# Reproduction for bead inc-gatz: a creature that walks into a field whose
# effect enlarges it to a size with a FaceRadius is relinked at the wrong
# square (Thing::Move relinks after EV_FIELDON; Values.cpp:1798 PlaceNear moved
# it meanwhile). Needs the scratch module with tools/fixtures/inc-gatz-growth.irh
# appended (tools/check_inc_gatz.sh builds it).

@include chargen.keys
@until "HP:" ESC

w y
@choose "Genocide Everything"
@until "HP:" ESC

# Stay on the starting level (depth 1): a wizard-mode depth change lands the
# player by a fall behind a modal "Press [ENTER]" prompt, and which level a
# seed generates shifts whenever a resource is appended to lib/. Do not depend
# on that level: lay plain ground ("Loose-Packed Earth": dry, walkable) under
# the player and the two squares east, so whatever the generator put there
# (deep water, a wall) cannot block the walk below.
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
ENTER
@choose "Loose-Packed Earth"
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT ENTER
@choose "Loose-Packed Earth"
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT*2 ENTER
@choose "Loose-Packed Earth"

# Put solid rock north of the square the player will step onto. A Huge mover
# cannot stand where its bulk touches rock, so the growth makes PlaceNear move
# it to another square: that move is the divergence the fix guards. Without
# rock in reach, PlaceNear leaves the mover where it is and no relink goes
# wrong, so the check would pass with the fix removed.
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT UP ENTER
@choose "Solid Rock"

# Summon the growth archon two squares east. Its field (ADJUST_CIRC, radius
# 1) covers the square one east of the player, so stepping there enters it:
# that Thing::Move is the path whose relink the fix guards. Dump the screen
# while the "You swell enormously!" message is up, so the check can see the
# field was entered.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Celestials"
@choose "gatz growth archon"
RIGHT*2 ENTER
@dump:summoned

RIGHT
@dump:step1
@quit
